[h1]Turn every meal into a kitchen story[/h1]
Cooks gather tools, diners fetch settings, meals remember their journey, and somebody washes up.

[b]RimWorld 1.6[/b]

[img]https://images.steamusercontent.com/ugc/13442990941541857998/74B79873E49B4696E8CA93F846362ED84CA10DA9/[/img]

[h1]What changes[/h1]
[list]
[*][b]Stuff-aware kitchenware[/b] - Material, quality and dirt matter.
[*][b]Physical meal service[/b] - Most meals use reusable kitchenware.
[*][b]Dishwashing and sanitation[/b] - Used gear returns dirty for washing.
[*][b]Ingredient preparation[/b] - Faster cooking, shorter shelf life.
[*][b]Cooperative cooking[/b] - Linked cooks assist the chef.
[*][b]Culinary quality[/b] - Ingredients, skill, tools and service shape servings.
[*][b]Meal temperature and reheating[/b] - Pawns prefer microwaves, then stoves and campfires; heaters slowly thaw meals as a last resort.
[*][b]Dining standards[/b] - Wealth and rank raise expectations.
[*][b]Travel, guests, children and patient feeding[/b] - Sensible tableware for each.
[*][b]Nutrient paste[/b] - Bring a plate; paste can be an ingredient.
[*][b]Trade and world-generated meals[/b] - Outsiders may pack tableware.
[/list]

[img]https://images.steamusercontent.com/ugc/10690968686544202098/07F935B974C098924B64F63F2B2D009BEDA574D9/[/img]

[h1]New things[/h1]
[list]
[*][b]Primitive stone cookware set[/b] - Rough early-game pots and pans.
[*][b]Cookware set[/b] - Reusable pots and pans in many materials.
[*][b]Glitterworld cookware set[/b] - Rare self-cleaning gear.
[*][b]Plate and adobe plate[/b] - Reusable plates in many materials.
[*][b]Cutlery setting[/b] - Stackable utensils.
[*][b]Chef's knife set[/b] - Personal tools for cooks.
[*][b]Prepared ingredients[/b] - Faster cooking, short shelf life.
[/list]

[img]https://images.steamusercontent.com/ugc/12178242142684133388/6F61AD9217541F194847E28F8AE5DF0EA13A2426/[/img]

[h1]New buildings[/h1]
[list]
[*][b]Dishwasher[/b] - Cleans batches and resumes after interruptions.
[*][b]Industrial dishwasher[/b] - Handles busy kitchens.
[*][b]Ingredient prep station[/b] - Prepares raw food.
[*][b]Sauce station[/b] - Adds a linked cook's skill and speed.
[*][b]Meat station[/b] - Adds a specialist cook.
[*][b]Vegetable station[/b] - Adds skilled hands.
[*][b]Pastry station[/b] - Supports demanding recipes.
[*][b]Microwave[/b] - Reheats meals on tables or workbenches.
[/list]

[img]https://images.steamusercontent.com/ugc/16964579834434312533/00D2F7C366EAC7AFD66D96B35BFBC728F33AEDD6/[/img]

[h1]Little rules that make it feel alive[/h1]
Pemmican and survival meals stay hand food. Animals never steal forks. Meals return only their own tableware. Dirty tools work in an emergency.

[img]https://images.steamusercontent.com/ugc/14279485497011088196/1394EBA094EB853E3E71249E8F3B581900348911/[/img]

[h1]Required Mods[/h1]
[list]
[*][b][url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=2009463077]Harmony[/url][/b] - The only required third-party mod; load it before Core.
[/list]

[img]https://images.steamusercontent.com/ugc/11716376724861319635/B9A0FEB55759677B102509FFD8D30A4C149D81EA/[/img]

[h1]Recommended Mods[/h1]
[list]
[*][b][url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=836308268]Dubs Bad Hygiene[/url][/b] - Adds plumbed dishwashers and preferred sinks.
[*][b][url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3210544395]Processor Framework[/url][/b] - Powers the dishwasher cycle and its visible progress.
[*][b][url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=1561769193]Common Sense[/url][/b] - Diners and nurses tidy used place settings after meals.
[*][b][url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=1279012058]Pick Up And Haul[/url][/b] - Collects and returns nearby dishes in batches.
[*][b][url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3071298014]Stack Gap[/url][/b] - Compatible with personal cooks and Pick Up And Haul.
[*][b][url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3486264784]SBZ Fridge[/url][/b] - Loads after Adaptive Storage Framework ([url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3033901359]Workshop page[/url]); meals chill or freeze quickly, thaw slowly, and lose more quality after freezing.
[/list]

[h1]Optional Mods[/h1]
[list]
[*][b]Royalty[/b] - Nobles demand finer meals and tableware.
[*][b]Biotech[/b] - Self-feeding children dine normally; babies do not.
[*][b]Expanded Materials - Metals[/b] - Adds suitable metal choices.
[*][b]Expanded Materials - Masonry[/b] - Adds suitable stone choices.
[*][b]Ceramics (Continued)[/b] - Adds porcelain plates.
[*][b]Simply Sublime ABS Polymer[/b] - Adds plastic kitchenware.
[*][b]Gastronomy[/b] - With Cash Register, waiters serve and clear settings.
[*][b]Hospitality[/b] - Guests borrow colony tableware sensibly.
[*][b]Cook for Yourself[/b] - Personal cooks gather their own tools.
[*][b]Variety Matters[/b] - Variety and culinary quality work together.
[*][b]Vanilla Food Variety Expanded[/b] - Added ingredients remain in meal history.
[*][b]Dynamic Meal Texture Replacer[/b] - Meal looks survive plating and saves.
[*][b]Food Texture Variety[/b] - Core loads before main; matching VCE add-ons retain meal art.
[*][b]Vanilla Expanded Framework[/b] - Supports compatible Vanilla Expanded food mods.
[*][b]Vanilla Textures Expanded - Variations[/b] - With Vanilla Expanded Framework, adds variations.
[*][b]Vanilla Nutrient Paste Expanded[/b] - With Vanilla Expanded Framework, paste uses plates.
[*][b]Adaptive Meal Bill[/b] - Adaptive bills use the same kitchen rules.
[*][b]Meals on Wheels Continued[/b] - Delivery preserves tableware handling.
[*][b]Replimat / Replimat Meals[/b] - Replimat loads before its Meals add-on; diners bring plates.
[*][b]Vanilla Cooking Expanded[/b] - With Vanilla Expanded Framework (and Fishing for Sushi), meals join.
[*][b]Fried Meals[/b] - With Harmony and Vanilla Expanded Framework, meals join.
[*][b]Fast Meals[/b] - Fast recipes keep their quick-food identity.
[*][b]Prioritize Meals over Preserved Foods[/b] - Food priorities stay intact.
[*][b]RimCuisine 2[/b] - Processor Framework loads before Core, then modules.
[*][b]Meal Printer[/b] - Printed meals receive safe plate handling.
[*][b]RimFridge[/b] - Meals chill or freeze quickly, thaw slowly, and lose more quality after freezing; plates stay attached.
[*][b]Adaptive Storage Framework[/b] - Stored meals keep attached tableware.
[*][b]Overcooked Meals[/b] - Burnt results keep sensible plate rules.
[*][b]No Vanilla Meals[/b] - Removed vanilla meals leave no broken rules.
[*][b]Thermodynamics - Hot Meals[/b] - Its temperature system and microwave take over.
[/list]

[h1]Languages[/h1]
English, German, Spanish, French, Simplified Chinese and Russian are included.

[h1]Author's Note[/h1]
This mod was completely developed by AI, supervised by me. I am a professional software developer and wanted to try using my experience and processes with agentic engineering for developing mods. A big focus was on creating frameworks for maintainability, testability and performance testing, which should help with maintaining compatibility with many mods and future RimWorld versions. I'll probably open-source the framework later if it proves itself, so other modders can use it as well. The mod does not generate AI content while RimWorld is running.

The mod itself was chosen for its complexity. It is a sweet spot of adding assets and new behaviours, but also having to be compatible with many other mods and DLC. It is a proving ground for more complex mods in the future. Be aware that while this is tested more thoroughly on a technical level than most, if not all, other mods, it is playtested much less heavily than usual. Feel free to comment on the balancing and any other oddities you encounter. I'll read them and implement the feedback.
